    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a derived, read-only Luhn check digit computed over the digits of `customerCode`, mirroring how other derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `locality`, etc.) are produced at response-mapping time.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a small utility whose `of(String)` computes the Luhn check digit over the digits in a string, ignoring non-digit separators. The algorithm matches the test's `luhn()` exactly (right-to-left, doubling from the rightmost digit, `(10 - sum%10) % 10`).\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer, 0\u20139, `readOnly`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `checkDigit` that calls `CheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())`.\n\nThe target test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which POSTs an owner, reads it back via GET, and asserts `checkDigit == luhn(customerCode)` \u2014 passes, and the full `mvn test` build is green.",
